Z||000010||william_thorniii||10-26-2000||08:21 AM||||Friends,<P>The Opel Speedster is merely a rebodied Lotus Elise.  The suspension is Lotus, because everything with the exception of the body is Lotus.  The problem is that Opel (GM) wants to import it, but Lotus does not want to compromise its small batch manufacturing.  Since Lotus is now owned by an asian company, they very well might sell the design/manufacturing rights to GM, but it is highly unlikely.<P>The interesting thing is that the 4-cyl engine used in both the Lotus and the Opel is the GM eco-tech engine.  Furthermore the Lotus Elise is far too light to be imported.  It is NOT street-legal in the US as it weighs in at under 1000kg.  This yields a VERY impressive hp/# ratio.  In fact I would expect times around 6 seconds to 60mph and near 12 seconds to 100.<P>GM would need to get it crash test certified and add all the necessary safety equipment such as air bags, door beams, etc.  All this aside, every time any car mag mentions the Opel, there is talk of bringing this car over... this has been going on for over three years now since the car first hit the circuit.  Yet the rumours are ALWAYS denied.  For true sports car fans, check out the new Lotus M250 and mk2000 on the Lotus website.  <P>I hate to poop on your parade but...<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||13
