Z||000025||saleenfiero||10-26-2000||05:56 PM||||Okay, I may be asking for it.  But am I the only one who really doesn't care is the fiero comes back?  Don't get me wrong, I love them as much as anybody, but does anybody really expect to get a car even resembling the spirit of the original?  The fiero has its time and really, it seems as though its collectors value and exclusiveness in years to come will be damaged by bringing the name back.  Sure you'll either get a lotus elise with kicker styling and the fiero name, BUT, you'll also pay lotus elise price.<BR>OR you'll get a toyota celica clone, cheap priced, and all the wonderful comealongs with that j/k.<BR>I'm sure GM isn't going to pour resources into another sports cars with the vette redesign, nomad resurrection and other launches so close.  Remember, the North America has forgotten sports cars and invested in SUV's instead.<BR>Let the fiero keep its timeless and established image and just call the new speedster the New Gremlin.||||reg||9
Z||000026||william_thorniii||10-26-2000||06:26 PM||||Saleen,<P>No worries.  GM has repeatedly stated that nothing will ever carry the Fiero moniker.  That was definitely not a difficult decision for them since the public still has a bad taste in their mouth about the word Fiero.  Unfounded or not.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||2
Z||000027||Songman||10-26-2000||08:37 PM||||WT, GM is going to market another great two-seater. Unfortunately for Fiero fans it will not be a mid-engine design.  Personally, I love the Cadillac Evoq and can't wait to get my hands on one. Cadillac says that this car shares the platform with the newly designed 2002 C6 Corvette. The Evoq has been around for a year or two now, but as far as I can tell, no one has seen anything of this new 2002 Corvette.... Anybody?||||reg||1
Z||000028||Pontiaddict||10-26-2000||11:30 PM||||Guess what Tigger, The People who designed the Aztec, are the some ones who are making the C6 Corvette. ||||reg||1
