Z||000030||87ECO5||10-27-2000||06:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>The Evoq has been around for a year or two now, but as far as I can tell, no one has seen anything of this new 2002 Corvette.... Anybody?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>GM has done a pretty good job of keeping the lid on the C6 project (BTW, I believe the C6 debut, barring any unforeseen production problems, is scheduled for 2004 - after the 2003 50th anniversary).  The latest word is that it will be an evolutionary change to the current C5 platform; similar in styling (minus the hidden headlights!?!?!?) and using the current generation's LS-1/6 powerplants.<P>I believe it was the August issue of MT that had an "artist's rendition" of the new car on the cover.  It was already being criticized in the December issue by folks saying the designers spent too much time looking at the front end of a Ferrari 360.  One guy even had the nerve of saying the drawing looked like the result of a 360 and a Pontiac Sunfire making love - AUGH!!!<P>To get back on-topic ... I think Pontiac SHOULD bring this car over here and I think they SHOULD slap a Fiero name on it.  Good press is good press.  A quick, reliable, well-balanced, able to compete with its competitors, new Fiero will boost our Fiero's image.  Yes, we'd then have the argument from the knowledgeable folks saying it's not the same car, but the less-in-touch idiots (the ones that give us the typical "unsafe", "plastic-bodied Chevette", or "doesn't it catch fire?" comments) would be hushed!||||reg||1
Z||000031||william_thorniii||10-27-2000||08:36 AM||||Songman,<BR>Give me a call when you get your hands on one!  I will personally drive down to TN just to look at it!  The only problem with the Evoq is that it is estimated at being priced in the mid 70's.  I am looking for a house in that range.  I love the Evoq though especially the thought of an integrated Supercharger mounted to an LS-1!  Funny thing is that when the car debuted (that's not a word!?) at the Detroit Int'l Auto Show back in 97, it was mentioned that it was based on the C5.  Probably just one of those discrepencies between the show car and the production car.  Unfortunately, I think Cadillac will re-learn the lesson they got from the Allante on this project, as much as I hate to say that.  Most folks would never think of dropping 70 G's for a Caddy... sad but true.<BR> <BR>Cheever2,<BR>Does GM now only have 1 design house for domestic vehicles?  Last I heard they were still trying to break them up by division... performance car, luxo car, truck, etc.  Say it ain't so!<P>87ECO5,<BR>I agree with you brother... but they won't <P>:~(<BR> <BR>William T. Thorn, III<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000032||Tigger||10-27-2000||08:57 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pontiaddict:<BR><B>Guess what Tigger, The People who designed the Aztec, are the some ones who are making the C6 Corvette. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I know, scary isn't it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
